# Keep machine-written data files byte-stable across platforms.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout rewrites committed LF files to CRLF on
# disk. For data that a script compares byte-for-byte before deciding whether to
# write, that is not cosmetic: scripts/pull_nfl_data.py skips a file whose content
# matches, and CRLF conversion made every file look changed on every local run, so
# the skip never fired.
#
# -text means "store and check out exactly these bytes".
*.json -text
*.csv -text

# The pages and scripts are fine either way, but pinning them keeps diffs clean
# when the repo is edited from both Windows and a CI runner.
*.html text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
